  "interpretation": "Across the full georeferenced GloPL sampling frame, experimental pollen limitation increases with distance from the seeded major continental landmasses under the frozen primary model, and both frozen sensitivities retain a positive global direction. However, the supplemental-only sensitivity is not independently supported, the predeclared northern-midlatitude versus tropical service-gradient prediction is not supported and points in the opposite interaction direction, and the four-context comparison is structurally unavailable because GloPL contains no northern-high-latitude sites under the frozen latitude definition. This supports a broad isolation-associated pollen-limitation association, not the context-specific common upstream mechanism proposed for the Chapter 1 plant H2 response.",
